From fea4ef50e21f4758985512a8ad60cb12dd27d26a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds-bootstrap <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:20:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] comm_state_private: take MATHRandContext32 from the port's
 rand.h

src/comm_state_private.h:75 repeats the MATHRandContext32 definition that the
port's hgss/compat/include/nitro/math/rand.h also provides. global.h includes
<nitro.h> before the private header's copy, so GCC sees two definitions of the
struct, and because the two are separate types "comm_state.c:79: conflicting
types for MATHRandContext32". MWCC never sees rand.h (HGSS has no such
header), so its single copy is fine on the DS.

Under SDK_PORT_3DS skip the local copy and use rand.h's, the same fix 1201
applied to the CRC structs. The #else keeps the original text.

gcc-10 -E -P of the header without SDK_PORT_3DS: byte-identical (371822 bytes
both). comm_state.c is checked with 1515, which finishes its other errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/comm_state_private.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/comm_state_private.h b/src/comm_state_private.h
index 6efa0aa..cb3a026 100644
--- a/src/comm_state_private.h
+++ b/src/comm_state_private.h
@@ -72,11 +72,15 @@ void Comm_EnableKeySync(void);
 u16 Comm_GetLocalNetId(void);
 BOOL Comm_HasLinkError(void);
 
+#ifndef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// HGSS keeps its own copy; the port's nitro/math/rand.h declares the same
+// struct and global.h includes <nitro.h> before this line.
 typedef struct {
     u64 x;
     u64 mul;
     u64 add;
 } MATHRandContext32;
+#endif
 
 void CommRandom_Init(MATHRandContext32 *seed);
 void Comm_FreeCommandTable(void);
